---
import Beta from '../layouts/Beta.astro';
import registry from '../../../../content/coverage-registry.json';
import { collections, episodes, areas } from '../lib/library';
const mahabharata = registry.works.mahabharata;
const totalSources = Object.values(mahabharata.evidence).reduce((sum, count) => sum + count, 0);
---
<Beta title="Coverage">
  <header class="beta-intro"><h1>What you can read</h1><p class="lede">The companion library has {episodes.length} annotated epic and Purāṇic episodes across {collections.length} collections. The atlas chapter counts are tracked separately below.</p></header>
  <div class="reading-width">
    <section class="beta-band"><h2>Mahābhārata Atlas</h2>
      <p>{mahabharata.books.length} parva guides and {mahabharata.indexed.toLocaleString('en')} indexed BORI chapters.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>{mahabharata.annotated} have a chapter-specific annotation.</li>
        <li>{mahabharata.sceneLinkedOnly} additional chapters link to one or more atlas scenes.</li>
        <li>{mahabharata.indexOnly.toLocaleString('en')} provide a locator and primary source.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>{mahabharata.scenes} scenes, {mahabharata.battleDays} battle days and {totalSources} dating and context records. Three author-reported bounds can be combined. The observer sky uses modern samples. The historical transit comparison remains prereview.</p><p><a href="/mahabharata/">Open the atlas</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="beta-band"><h2>Rāmāyaṇa Atlas</h2>
      <p>{registry.works.ramayana.books.length} kāṇḍas and {registry.works.ramayana.indexed} indexed Baroda sargas.
        {registry.works.ramayana.annotated} have a chapter annotation, and {registry.works.ramayana.indexOnly} provide a locator and primary source.</p>
      <a href="/ramayana/">Open the Rāmāyaṇa atlas</a>
    </section>
    <section class="beta-band"><h2>Swarajya and Maratha history</h2>
      <p>{registry.maratha.datedRecords} dated records across {registry.maratha.periods} historical periods, {registry.maratha.historyPlaces} location entries and {registry.maratha.logisticsDossiers} fort or port investigations. The Raigad terrain lesson still has {registry.maratha.terrainSamples} elevation samples.</p>
      <a href="/swarajya/history/">Open the documented changes</a>
    </section>
    <ul class="search-list">
      {collections.map((collection) => {
        const entries = episodes.filter((episode) => episode.collection === collection.id);
        const chapters = [...new Set(entries.flatMap((episode) => episode.passages.map((passage) => passage.chapter)))];
        return <li><a href={`/epics/${collection.id}/`}>{collection.title}</a>
          <p>{entries.length} {entries.length === 1 ? 'episode' : 'episodes'} · {chapters.join(', ')}</p></li>;
      })}
    </ul>
    <p>These are excerpts and paraphrases tied to source locators. Independent editorial review, full-book coverage, and regional retellings are pending.</p>
    <section class="beta-band">
      <h2>Beyond the stories</h2>
      <ul class="reading-list">{areas.slice(1).map((area) => <li><a href={area.url}>{area.title}</a> · {area.text}</li>)}</ul>
      <p>The modern transit benchmark is recorded separately. A historical result for Arundhatī–Vasiṣṭha remains unavailable pending independent review.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Beta>
